<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Budget's cross-section surface, carved into its own leaf project because one of its
    consumers is still in Base: TicketQueryService (Humans.Application) reads the active year
    to compute the break-even summary. A Contracts/ *folder* inside Humans.Budget would
    therefore make Base reference a section and cycle (design §15.5b,
    memory/architecture/section-project-cycle-fix.md). The second Base consumer,
    TicketingBudgetSyncJob, moved into Humans.Budget/Contracts/ at G5 lane 5b-3
    (nobodies-collective/Humans#866), taking Humans.Infrastructure's reference to this leaf
    with it.

    It holds the read surface the other sections actually call — four methods out of
    IBudgetService's forty — plus the DTOs and the two enums that appear in their
    signatures. Everything else Budget does (year/group/category/line-item CRUD, the audit
    log, the cash-flow and VAT projections, the ticketing projection parameters) has no
    consumer outside the section and stays internal to Humans.Budget.

    References Humans.Interfaces only — the bottom of the graph.
  -->

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Humans.Interfaces\Humans.Interfaces.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="NodaTime" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
